"## Summary\n\nSecops follow-up 15: AT29's manual grant withdrawal through `revokeMemberGrant` (#297), the shared node write adopted at secops' six sites, and one live AT29 transport run.\n- **Session:** launched 20:17 EST on 2026-11-03, and delivered at 21:02.\n- **Model:** codex `gpt-6-astra`.\n- **Size:** 7 commits and 150 owned files, +238,920/\u22122,411. Most of it is records: the D-098 archive of 112 root records and the new run's records. The largest file is 0.8 MB, and the total is 7.7 MB.\n- **Checks:**\n  - merge-tree clean on current `main`; prepush-scan clean; owned-check passes.\n  - **The orchestrator reran these** on a scratch tree, current `main` (`ff5efb69`) with this branch merged in. All pass:\n    - `make -f mk/at-secops.mk at-secops-lint`, `at-secops-test` and `at-secops-build`;\n    - `go vet -tags e2e ./tests/e2e/...`;\n    - `go test ./tests/handover/...`;\n    - the committed-evidence hygiene tests in `tests/e2e` and `tests/netlab`;\n    - `make go-lint`, gofmt and `git diff --check`.\n- **Scope:** one live run in the lane's own namespace, with no rerun and no reservation. Zero owned Docker objects at the end.\n- **A merge-gate fix, 21:21\u201321:26.** The merge queue's first attempt stopped on the merged tree at `make -f mk/e2e.mk e2e-lint`. Its `staticcheck -tags e2e` reported `activeTransport11` and `quietTransport11` unused (U1000).\n  - **Why:** they are built with `e2e`, and their only callers need `e2e && integration`. The lane's own lint passes both tags, so it never saw this. The orchestrator's earlier check ran the lane lint, not `e2e-lint`.\n  - **The fix:** `99d1d5b3` adds `TestAT29_TransportActivityPredicates` under `e2e` alone: six synthetic sample pairs that assert both predicates as they are today. Neither predicate changed, and no live run was taken.\n  - **The orchestrator reran,** on current `main` with updater 24, this branch and handover 42 merged in: `e2e-lint`, `at-secops-lint`, `at-secops-test`, `at-isolation-lint` and the new test. All pass.\n  - **The second queue attempt,** 21:36\u201321:40, passed every gate on the merged tree. It stopped before pushing, because the orchestrator had not refreshed the PR title file after the fix. Requeued after agent-core 48, with the gates rerun on the merged tree.\n\n**The orchestrator's reading.**\n- **The live run:** `35116d25`, on `dd052c60` (#441), 20:41\u201320:52 EST. The Go test passed in 622.6 s.\n- **The four runnable AT29 sub-cases pass:** grant expiry, lease expiry, device revoke and manual withdrawal.\n- **AT29 overall stays blocked,** only on `guest_clock_rollback`. That needs a disposable guest whose clock can be set on its own, which is an operator resource.\n- **Manual withdrawal, through the public API only:**\n  - **The bound is \u00a716.5's online revocation starting target,** 60 s, counted from the request. The predicate takes the earlier of that and the observed lease's end. In this run the 60 s target came first, so the cutoff is the withdrawal's own, not the lease's.\n  - **Cutoff:** the operation completes, and both original transports, the established TCP/9446 connection and the authenticated UDP/9445 socket, first show quiet 2.48 s after the request. A new flow gets no HTTP 200.\n  - **With the Agent killed,** both stay quiet and the watchdog keeps running. TCP stays at 11 replies while attempts go from 83 to 93; UDP stays at 11 while attempts go from 155 to 176.\n  - **Recovery:** a new grant's applied ACK (generation 22) brings fresh TCP and UDP replies.\n  - **Restoration:** the member's original finite standing comes back through public APIs, on every path, early returns included. An uncleared D-077 fence is rejected offline.\n- **A limit of the lease-expiry pass,** which this follow-up did not change. It records `continued_before_expiry` as true, over a 3 s sample after control stopped, but does not assert it. A hanging control plane, r28's H-1, is not exercised. AT29's control-loss continuity case is a later